    id: "sc-180", athlete_id: "yamasaki", order: 5, stage: "rebirth",
    title: "Guardian of Yokohama Once More — The Mound Is Where I Belong",
    body: "Following his Olympic resurrection, Yasuaki reclaimed his place as the closer of the Yokohama DeNA BayStars. The \"Yasuaki Jump\" returned to Yokohama Stadium. That moment of unity between fans and player was alive once more.\n\n\"The mound is where I belong. I won't give it up to anyone.\" Because he once nearly lost that place, those words carry an unshakeable weight.\n\nThe man who turned a slump into a gift. The suffering in the minors broadened his pitching repertoire, forged his mental toughness, and deepened his strategic duels with hitters. The result was a pitcher of far greater completeness than the one who had existed before the slump.\n\nThe boy from Arakawa Ward, raised single-handedly by his Vietnamese-born mother, experienced defeat and resurrection in the world of professional baseball, and grew into a \"true closer.\" The sight of him pumping both arms on the mound is proof for all people that you can claw your way back from the very bottom.",
    year_label: "2021–",
