    body: "With her jaw wired shut and unable to eat properly, Ueno did not stop. She could not throw. She could not eat. But her legs still worked — with that determination, she poured all her energy into lower body and core training while waiting for her jaw to heal.\n\n\"The day my jaw was broken, my softball career was reset and started anew.\"\n\nThrough the rehabilitation process, Ueno confronted her thirty-seven-year-old body head-on. Not the power pitching of her youth, but a new style built on seasoned command and pinpoint accuracy with her off-speed pitches. The injury was driving her evolution.\n\nHead coach Reika Utsugi described what she witnessed: \"She's like a cyborg. Even with a broken jaw, all she thought about was getting back on the mound.\"",
